AC5 / MUTATION PROOF -- FAIL
Mutations were applied one at a time in SC/mut; the log is SC/mutations-js.log. The copy was restored and `diff -rq` against the snapshot was clean.
Killed:
- (a) re-add isError=false: KILLED ("a rejected retargeted 4xx still swaps but reports failure…").
- (b) early return in the new responseError listener: KILLED (4 tests).
- (c) drop reportValidityOfForms: KILLED ("enables htmx's native reportValidity()").
- (d) drop role="alert" from renderError: KILLED. Output: "--- FAIL: TestRenderError … handlers_test.go:804" and "schedule_month_form_test.go:858".
- R1: wrapper role re-added on the income slot: KILLED (:833). Wrapper role re-added on the OOB big-ticket clear: KILLED (:872/:876). Inline node wrapped in a second role=alert: KILLED. Fallback without a role: KILLED.
- R2, full revert to the attempt-1 errorHost: KILLED (poll + body tests).
- R3, drop the __wfText short-circuit: KILLED.
- R4, drop the nodeType guard: KILLED. Fallback uses innerHTML instead of textContent: KILLED.
- Also killed: drop clear-on-success, drop the HX-Retarget skip, drop the /whatif path scope.
SURVIVED (all 10 node tests pass; the Go suite never touches base.js):
- M1: in errorHost, `if (!host && INTERACTIVE_TAGS[elt.tagName] && hasOwnHxVerb(elt))` changed to `if (!host)`. This drops the user-initiated-only rule and falls back to parentNode for any form-less elt. Result: pass=10 fail=0.
- M2: `return isForbiddenHost(host) ? null : host;` changed to `return host;`. This drops the html/body/main/grid refusal. Result: pass=10 fail=0.
Why both survive: tests (ii) and (iii) place their sentinel under a host that BOTH guards reject (the poll inside a data-wf-layout-grid div; body under html). Removing either guard alone therefore changes nothing they can see.
Test (ii)'s own comment says "Mutation this kills: errorHost() falling back to `elt.parentNode` for ANY form-less elt". That claim is false: it is exactly M1.
M1 is not an equivalent mutant. SC/e2e-loader.cjs served base.js with M1 (via page.route) against the real branch server on a cold load. The real #whatif-async-loader (hx-trigger="load") got a 500 from /whatif/results-full, and the alert "Analysis failed: loader probe" was inserted into #whatif-results. The unmutated base.js leaves it alone (inline=[]). This is an R2 violation that the suite cannot detect.
MISSING (the worker adds these):
1. A test where a sentinel (hx-trigger load/every) sits under a NON-forbidden parent (a plain div, or #whatif-results like the real async loader) and asserts no insertion. This kills M1.
2. A test where an eligible trigger (e.g. a button with its own hx-verb) sits directly in body, main or a data-wf-layout-grid element and asserts no insertion. This kills M2.
Each test must pass against the current base.js and fail under its mutant.

