OBSERVATIONS (not the basis of the FAIL; for the lead/backlog)
O1 (R1 coverage). Adding role="alert" to the healthcare slot (#whatif-add-healthcare-error, healthcare-card.html:24) survives the Go suite (ok 9.633s). The nesting test's kinds/OOB lists cover income/expense/onetime/bigticket only. Behaviour today is correct (1 alert).
O2 (R4 by the letter). buildErrorNode parses every body with innerHTML and never consults Content-Type.
- A text/plain body that starts with a tag (probe: '<b>plain text…</b>') is inserted as a <b> element with NO role and not via textContent.
- No current path reaches this: http.Error appears only in /whatif/state and /whatif/apply (API, no htmx caller) and /whatif/poll (sentinel, excluded).
O3 (R3 on the retargeted path). Two identical rejected Add Income submits insert a fresh role=alert node twice (SC/e2e-r3retarget.cjs: alertNodesInsertedSoFar 1 then 2). This is htmx's own innerHTML swap on an explicit user resubmit. At base the second submit is impossible because the form is wiped. Lead to rule on whether R3 covers this.
O4. The host for a form-less control is its parent, which is often a flex row. The Monte Carlo error sits beside the "Monte Carlo Simulation" heading and the Re-run button inside `flex items-center justify-between` (SC/5xx-mc-br.png). This is layout, for checker-a11y and the backlog.
O5. Retargeted 5xx still show nowhere: 4 renderRetargetedError(…500…) sites, e.g. handlers_income_expense.go:53. This is pre-existing (WS4.1 O1).
O6. WS4.1 O3 (sitewide reportValidityOfForms combined with the WS1 step=1000 cost-basis field) was carried forward. It was not re-run this attempt.
